.TH "ROTBYTE\-HEALTHCHECKS" "7" "2026\-11\-07" "rotbyte 1.3.0" "rotbyte Manual"
.SH NAME
rotbyte\-healthchecks \- monitor rotbyte scans with healthchecks.io
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set up \f[CR]rotbyte \-\-notify healthchecks\f[R] to monitor your scans
with \c
.UR https://healthchecks.io
healthchecks.io
.UE \c
\ or a self\-hosted \c
.UR https://github.com/healthchecks/healthchecks
Healthchecks
.UE \c
\ instance.
.PP
Email only speaks up when a scan runs.
healthchecks.io also tells you when scans \f[B]stop running\f[R]: a Mac
that\(cqs asleep or switched off, an unmounted volume, or a schedule
broken by an upgrade.
Every scan pings its check, so healthchecks.io notices when the pings
stop arriving.
.PP
This is a one\-time setup.
It works on its own or alongside email
(\f[CR]\-\-notify email,healthchecks\f[R]; see
\f[CR]rotbyte \-\-docs notify\f[R]).
.SS Quick start
.IP
.EX
rotbyte \-\-notify\-setup healthchecks
.EE
.PP
You\(cqll be prompted for:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Ping endpoint.\f[R] Press Enter to accept
\f[CR]https://hc\-ping.com\f[R].
For a self\-hosted instance, see Self\-hosted Healthchecks.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Ping key.\f[R] On healthchecks.io, open your project\(cqs
\f[B]Settings\f[R] page.
The ping key is listed there next to your project\(cqs API keys.
Create one if the project doesn\(cqt have one yet.
.PP
Setup then sends a test ping to confirm the key works and saves the
config.
.PP
\f[B]Setup session:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
$ rotbyte \-\-notify\-setup healthchecks

  Ping endpoint [https://hc\-ping.com]:
  Ping key:

  Testing ping key... ok.
  Config saved to /Users/you/Library/Application Support/rotbyte/notify.conf
  Ping key stored in keychain (account: healthchecks\(athc\-ping.com)
  A \(aqrotbyte\-setup\-test\(aq check was created to verify the key.
  It never alerts; delete it from the dashboard whenever you like.
.EE
.PP
The test ping creates a check named \f[CR]rotbyte\-setup\-test\f[R].
It only receives a \f[I]log\f[R] ping, which never changes a check\(cqs
status, so it stays in the \(lqnew\(rq state and never alerts.
You can delete it.
.PP
\f[B]Config location\f[R] (shared with email; each backend has its own
section):
.IP \(bu 2
macOS: \f[CR]\(ti/Library/Application Support/rotbyte/notify.conf\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Linux: \f[CR]\(ti/.config/rotbyte/notify.conf\f[R] (or
\f[CR]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rotbyte/notify.conf\f[R])
.IP \(bu 2
Windows: \f[CR]%USERPROFILE%\(rs.config\(rsrotbyte\(rsnotify.conf\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]Where the ping key is stored.\f[R] Like the SMTP password, it goes
into the platform credential store:
.IP \(bu 2
macOS: Keychain
.IP \(bu 2
Windows: Credential Manager
.IP \(bu 2
Linux: libsecret, via \f[CR]secret\-tool\f[R]
.PP
If none of these is available, the key is saved in
\f[CR]notify.conf\f[R] with \f[CR]0600\f[R] permissions and setup prints
a warning.
Treat the key as a secret: anyone who has it can ping your project\(cqs
checks, including sending fake \(lqsuccess\(rq pings.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS Usage
Add \f[CR]\-\-notify healthchecks\f[R] to any scan, or to
\f[CR]\-\-track\f[R] so every scheduled scan reports:
.IP
.EX
\f[I]# One\-off scan\f[R]
rotbyte \-\-check \-\-notify healthchecks /Volumes/Media

\f[I]# Scheduled scans, with both email and healthchecks.io\f[R]
rotbyte \-\-track \-\-every 1h \-\-full\-at 2h \-\-budget 2h \(rs
        \-\-notify email,healthchecks /Volumes/Media
.EE
.PP
\f[CR]rotbyte \-\-track\-setup\f[R] also asks whether to ping
healthchecks.io.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS How it works
\f[B]One check per directory and scan type.\f[R] Each tracked directory
gets two checks, one for quick scans and one for full scans:
.IP
.EX
rotbyte\-media\-quick\-1a2b3c4d     quick scans of /Volumes/Media
rotbyte\-media\-full\-1a2b3c4d      full re\-verifies (\-\-check / \-\-due)
.EE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Name part.\f[R] The directory name, folded to the characters
healthchecks.io allows in a slug.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Hash part.\f[R] The same 8\-character hash that names the
directory\(cqs launchd, systemd, or Task Scheduler jobs.
Two directories with the same name still get separate checks.
.PP
A broken nightly full scan can\(cqt hide behind healthy hourly quick
scans, because they report to different checks.
.PP
\f[B]Checks are created automatically\f[R] on their first ping, using
healthchecks.io\(cqs auto\-provisioning (\f[CR]?create=1\f[R]).
\f[CR]rotbyte \-\-track\f[R] prints the names of the checks it will use,
and \f[CR]rotbyte \-\-status\f[R] lists them for each tracked directory.
.PP
\f[B]Every run pings, whatever the outcome.\f[R] A run first sends a
\f[I]start\f[R] signal.
When it finishes, it pings with rotbyte\(cqs exit code: \f[CR]0\f[R]
marks the check up, anything else marks it down.
.PP
