.TE
.PP
\f[B]Start and result pings are paired\f[R] with a per\-run ID, so
healthchecks.io shows how long each scan took.
.PP
\f[B]Skipped scans are treated differently by type.\f[R] A quick scan
that fires during a long full scan finds the database locked and skips.
It counts as a run, so the quick\-scan check doesn\(cqt false\-alarm.
A full scan that\(cqs skipped only \f[I]logs\f[R] the skip.
Its check isn\(cqt reset, so a nightly full scan that keeps missing its
slot still goes down.
.PP
\f[B]Every ping carries the scan report\f[R] as its body, so the
check\(cqs event log shows what the scan found.
This is the same report the email contains, including counts, change
since the last run, and duration.
As with email, \f[B]file paths are never sent\f[R].
The report names the directory and host, and tells you to run
\f[CR]rotbyte \-\-report <dir>\f[R] on that machine to list the affected
files.
.PP
\f[B]Network trouble never affects the scan.\f[R] Each ping retries a
couple of times, then gives up with a warning on stderr.
rotbyte\(cqs exit code is never changed by a failed ping.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS Tune each check\(cqs period and grace time
New checks start with healthchecks.io\(cqs defaults: a \f[B]period of 1
day\f[R] and a \f[B]grace time of 1 hour\f[R].
Those defaults rarely fit:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]The period is wrong for quick scans.\f[R] With an hourly quick
scan, the check wouldn\(cqt notice a dead schedule for a day.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]The grace is too short for full scans.\f[R] rotbyte sends a start
signal, and healthchecks.io expects the matching result within the grace
time.
A full scan that runs longer than that is reported down while it\(cqs
still working.
.PP
\f[CR]rotbyte \-\-track\f[R] prints suggested values for the schedule it
just installed:
.IP
.EX
  healthchecks.io checks (created on first ping \(em then set these in the dashboard):
    rotbyte\-media\-quick\-1a2b3c4d
      Period 1 hour · Grace 1 hour (more if quick scans hash many new files)
    rotbyte\-media\-full\-1a2b3c4d
      Period 1 day · Grace 3 hours
.EE
.PP
The rules behind those suggestions:
.PP
