.PP
The check is created by its first ping, so it won\(cqt exist in the
dashboard until each scan type has run once.
Set the values after that.
For full scans you can use a \f[B]Cron\f[R] schedule in the dashboard
instead, such as \f[CR]0 2 * * *\f[R] in your time zone.
.PP
\f[B]A directory\(cqs very first scan\f[R] indexes every file, which can
take hours.
rotbyte skips the start signal on that run, so a fresh check isn\(cqt
marked down during the initial index.
The result ping at the end still creates the check and records the
outcome.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS Self\-hosted Healthchecks
At the \f[B]Ping endpoint\f[R] prompt, enter your instance\(cqs
\f[CR]PING_ENDPOINT\f[R] URL.
This is usually your site\(cqs address followed by \f[CR]/ping\f[R], for
example:
.IP
.EX
  Ping endpoint [https://hc\-ping.com]: https://hc.example.com/ping
.EE
.PP
Notes:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Copy it from your dashboard.\f[R] The endpoint is the part of any
check\(cqs ping URL before the UUID.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Trailing slash is optional.\f[R] rotbyte adds or strips it as
needed.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Recent version required.\f[R] The instance must support slug URLs
and auto\-provisioning (\f[CR]?create=1\f[R]).
On an older instance, setup\(cqs test ping fails with HTTP 404.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Plain \f[CB]http://\f[B] works but isn\(cqt encrypted.\f[R] The
ping key would cross the network in the clear, and setup warns you about
it.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Self\-hosted keeps less of each ping body.\f[R] It stores 10 kB per
ping by default (\f[CR]PING_BODY_LIMIT\f[R]), compared with 100 kB on
healthchecks.io.
rotbyte\(cqs reports are only a few hundred bytes, so they fit either
way.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS Reconfiguring
Run \f[CR]rotbyte \-\-notify\-setup healthchecks\f[R] again at any time
to change the endpoint or key.
Only the \f[CR][healthchecks]\f[R] section of \f[CR]notify.conf\f[R] is
replaced, so your email settings are kept.
Running \f[CR]\-\-notify\-setup email\f[R] likewise leaves the
healthchecks.io settings alone.
.PP
To stop pinging for a tracked directory, re\-run \f[CR]\-\-track\f[R]
for it without \f[CR]healthchecks\f[R] in \f[CR]\-\-notify\f[R].
.SS Troubleshooting
\f[B]\(lqTesting ping key\&...
failed.
Error: HTTP 404\(rq\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
The ping key wasn\(cqt recognized.
Copy it again from the project\(cqs Settings page, and make sure you
pasted the key itself, not a full ping URL.
.IP \(bu 2
On a self\-hosted instance, the server may be too old for
auto\-provisioning.
See Self\-hosted Healthchecks.
.PP
\f[B]\(lqTesting ping key\&...
failed.
Error: HTTP 400\(rq\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
The ping key is malformed, usually because only part of it was copied.
healthchecks.io ping keys are 22 characters.
Copy the key again.
.IP \(bu 2
If you entered a custom ping endpoint, check it as well.
.PP
\f[B]The full\-scan check goes down every night while the scan is
running\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
The grace time is shorter than the scan.
Raise it to at least your \f[CR]\-\-budget\f[R] plus an hour.
See Tune each check\(cqs period and grace time.
.PP
\f[B]A check goes down even though scans seem to run\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Run \f[CR]rotbyte \-\-status\f[R].
The \f[CR]Notify:\f[R] line should include \f[CR]healthchecks\f[R], and
the \f[CR]checks:\f[R] line names the checks the directory pings.
.IP \(bu 2
Look for \f[CR]Warning: healthchecks.io ping failed\f[R] in the
scheduled\-scan log:
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
macOS: \f[CR]\(ti/Library/Logs/rotbyte/\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Linux: \f[CR]journalctl \-\-user \-u \(aqrotbyte\-*\(aq\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Windows: \f[CR]%LOCALAPPDATA%\(rsrotbyte\(rslogs\(rs\f[R], or the
task\(cqs history in Task Scheduler
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\(lqhealthchecks.io config is unavailable\(rq in a scheduled\-scan
log\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR][healthchecks]\f[R] section is missing, or the ping key
couldn\(cqt be read from the credential store.
The scan still runs, but it can\(cqt ping.
Run \f[CR]rotbyte \-\-notify\-setup healthchecks\f[R] again.
